Everything is clear, concise, and verified. I am ready to write the response.# Missing `highBid` Update in `auctionDemo.returnHighestBidder` Causes Incorrect Winner Selection

The `auctionDemo` contract tracks all bids for a given `_tokenid` in the `auctionInfoData[_tokenid]` array and determines the auction winner and winning bid via two functions: `returnHighestBid(uint256 _tokenid)` and `returnHighestBidder(uint256 _tokenid)`.

In `returnHighestBid` (lines 65–83), the loop tracks the maximum active bid by updating both `highBid` and `index` whenever a higher active bid is encountered:
```solidity
if (auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid > highBid && auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].status == true) {
    highBid = auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid;
    index = i;
}
```

However, in `returnHighestBidder` (lines 87–100), `highBid` is initialized to `0` at line 88 and is never updated when the condition at line 91 holds:
```solidity
function returnHighestBidder(uint256 _tokenid) public view returns (address) {
    uint256 highBid = 0;
    uint256 index;
    for (uint256 i=0; i< auctionInfoData[_tokenid].length; i++) {
        if (auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid > highBid && auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].status == true) {
            index = i;
        }
    }
    if (auctionInfoData[_tokenid][index].status == true) {
            return auctionInfoData[_tokenid][index].bidder;
        } else {
            revert("No Active Bidder");
    }
}
```

Because `highBid` remains `0` across every iteration of the loop, the comparison `auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid > highBid` simply evaluates to `auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid > 0`. Every active non-zero bid in `auctionInfoData[_tokenid]` overwrites `index = i`, causing `returnHighestBidder` to return the address of the last active entry in the array rather than the entry with the highest bid amount.

This creates a direct inconsistency between `returnHighestBid(_tokenid)` (which returns the true highest active `bid` value) and `returnHighestBidder(_tokenid)` (which returns the last active `bidder`):
1. The `WinnerOrAdminRequired` modifier on `claimAuction` checks `msg.sender == returnHighestBidder(_tokenid)`, denying access to the actual highest bidder if a subsequent active entry exists with a lower bid.
2. In `claimAuction` (lines 107–119), the winning entry is matched using both values simultaneously:
   ```solidity
   if (auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bidder == highestBidder && auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].bid == highestBid && auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].status == true)
   ```
   When `returnHighestBidder(_tokenid)` and `returnHighestBid(_tokenid)` resolve to different entries with different bidders, no element in `auctionInfoData[_tokenid]` matches both `bidder == highestBidder` and `bid == highestBid`. All active bids fall into the `else if (auctionInfoData[_tokenid][i].status == true)` refund branch, the auctioned ERC721 token is never transferred, the auction owner receives no payout, and `auctionClaim[_tokenid]` is permanently set to `true`.

