Update `PaymentEscrow._settlePayment` to treat `OrderType.PAYEE` orders identically to `OrderType.PAY` orders when determining pro-rata and full payment settlements.

```solidity
    function _settlePayment(
        Item[] calldata items,
        OrderType orderType,
        address lender,
        address renter,
        uint256 start,
        uint256 end
    ) internal {
        // Calculate the time values.
        uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - start;
        uint256 totalTime = end - start;

        // Determine whether the rental order has ended.
        bool isRentalOver = elapsedTime >= totalTime;

        // Loop through each item in the order.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < items.length; ++i) {
            // Get the item.
            Item memory item = items[i];

            // Check that the item is a payment.
            if (item.isERC20()) {
                // Set a placeholder payment amount which can be reduced in the
                // presence of a fee.
                uint256 paymentAmount = item.amount;

                // Take a fee on the payment amount if the fee is on.
                if (fee != 0) {
                    // Calculate the new fee.
                    uint256 paymentFee = _calculateFee(paymentAmount);

                    // Adjust the payment amount by the fee.
                    paymentAmount -= paymentFee;
                }

                // Effect: Decrease the token balance. Use the payment amount pre-fee
                // so that fees can be taken.
                _decreaseDeposit(item.token, item.amount);

                // If its a PAY or PAYEE order but the rental hasn't ended yet.
                if ((orderType.isPayOrder() || orderType.isPayeeOrder()) && !isRentalOver) {
                    // Interaction: a PAY or PAYEE order which hasnt ended yet. Payout is pro-rata.
                    _settlePaymentProRata(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        lender,
                        renter,
                        elapsedTime,
                        totalTime
                    );
                }
                // If its a PAY or PAYEE order and the rental is over, or, if its a BASE order.
                else if (
                    ((orderType.isPayOrder() || orderType.isPayeeOrder()) && isRentalOver) ||
                    orderType.isBaseOrder()
                ) {
                    // Interaction: a pay, payee, or base order which has ended. Payout is in full.
                    _settlePaymentInFull(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        item.settleTo,
                        lender,
                        renter
                    );
                } else {
                    revert Errors.Shared_OrderTypeNotSupported(uint8(orderType));
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

findings.technical_details:
When a rental order is created and fulfilled via `Create.sol`, the ERC20 payment items are transferred to the `PaymentEscrow` module and tracked via `ESCRW.increaseDeposit(items[i].token, items[i].amount)`. However, neither `RentalOrder` nor `PaymentEscrow` records the protocol `fee` that was in effect when the order was signed and initiated.

Instead, when the rental is terminated via `Stop.stopRent` or `Stop.stopRentBatch`, execution calls `PaymentEscrow.settlePayment` / `PaymentEscrow.settlePaymentBatch`, which delegates to `PaymentEscrow._settlePayment` (`smart-contracts/src/modules/PaymentEscrow.sol`, lines 242–248):

```solidity
if (fee != 0) {
    // Calculate the new fee.
    uint256 paymentFee = _calculateFee(paymentAmount);

    // Adjust the payment amount by the fee.
    paymentAmount -= paymentFee;
}
```

Here, `_calculateFee(paymentAmount)` (line 88) computes `(amount * fee) / 10000` using the current storage value of `fee` at the moment of settlement.

This design creates two concrete issues for existing obligations:
1. **Retroactive fee modification on active rentals:** When the protocol admin updates `fee` via `Admin.setFee` (which permits setting `feeNumerator` up to `10000`, or 100%), the new fee rate is immediately applied to all currently active and unstopped rentals that were entered into under the previous fee rate.
2. **Settlement-timing arbitrage and griefing:** Because expired rentals remain unstopped until a transaction invokes `stopRent`, and anyone can stop an expired rental, a pending `setFee` transaction allows participants (or MEV searchers) to front-run or back-run the fee change when calling `stopRent`, changing the net payout received by the lender or renter.

findings.remediation:
Store the protocol `fee` active at the time of rental creation (either as a field in the `RentalOrder` struct whose hash is stored in `Storage`, or in a mapping keyed by `orderHash` in `PaymentEscrow`), and use that snapshotted fee during `_settlePayment`.

```solidity
// In RentalStructs.sol: include uint256 fee in RentalOrder (set from ESCRW.fee() during creation)
// In PaymentEscrow.sol:
    function _calculateFee(uint256 amount, uint256 orderFee) internal pure returns (uint256) {
        // Uses 10,000 as a denominator for the fee.
        return (amount * orderFee) / 10000;
    }
```

And in `PaymentEscrow._settlePayment`:

```solidity
                // Take a fee on the payment amount if the order fee is on.
                if (orderFee != 0) {
                    // Calculate the fee using the fee snapshotted at order creation.
                    uint256 paymentFee = _calculateFee(paymentAmount, orderFee);

                    // Adjust the payment amount by the fee.
                    paymentAmount -= paymentFee;
                }
```

findings.technical_details:
In the reNFT protocol, a `PAY` order allows a lender to deposit ERC20 tokens into `PaymentEscrow` to pay a renter for renting an NFT over a specified duration (`end - start`). According to the protocol specification, the lender of a `PAY` order can stop the rental early (before `endTimestamp`), in which case the escrowed ERC20 payment is split pro-rata between the renter (payment for `elapsedTime`) and the lender (refund for the remaining unused duration `totalTime - elapsedTime`).

However, in `PaymentEscrow._settlePayment` (`smart-contracts/src/modules/PaymentEscrow.sol`), the protocol fee is calculated and subtracted from the full `paymentAmount` (`item.amount`) at lines 242–248 before branching on whether the order is an active `PAY` order:

```solidity
uint256 paymentAmount = item.amount;

// Take a fee on the payment amount if the fee is on.
if (fee != 0) {
    // Calculate the new fee.
    uint256 paymentFee = _calculateFee(paymentAmount);

    // Adjust the payment amount by the fee.
    paymentAmount -= paymentFee;
}

// Effect: Decrease the token balance. Use the payment amount pre-fee
// so that fees can be taken.
_decreaseDeposit(item.token, item.amount);

// If its a PAY order but the rental hasn't ended yet.
if (orderType.isPayOrder() && !isRentalOver) {
    // Interaction: a PAY order which hasnt ended yet. Payout is pro-rata.
    _settlePaymentProRata(
        item.token,
        paymentAmount,
        lender,
        renter,
        elapsedTime,
        totalTime
    );
}
```

When `_settlePaymentProRata` is subsequently called with the fee-adjusted `paymentAmount`, `_calculatePaymentProRata` computes:
- $\text{renterAmount} \approx \text{item.amount} \times (1 - \frac{\text{fee}}{10000}) \times \frac{\text{elapsedTime}}{\text{totalTime}}$
- $\text{lenderAmount} \approx \text{item.amount} \times (1 - \frac{\text{fee}}{10000}) \times \frac{\text{totalTime} - \text{elapsedTime}}{\text{totalTime}}$

Because the fee is deducted before the pro-rata calculation rather than only from the renter's earned share, the lender's refund (`lenderAmount`) is also reduced by the protocol `fee` percentage. The protocol fee should only apply to the actual rental payment earned by the renter (`renterAmount`), while the unspent portion of the deposit returned to the lender is a refund and must not be taxed.

findings.remediation:
For pro-rata settlements (`orderType.isPayOrder() && !isRentalOver`), calculate the pro-rata split on the full `item.amount` first, and apply the protocol fee only to the `renterAmount` (the earned payment portion) while refunding the full `lenderAmount` to the lender.

```solidity
    function _settlePaymentProRata(
        address token,
        uint256 amount,
        address lender,
        address renter,
        uint256 elapsedTime,
        uint256 totalTime
    ) internal {
        // Calculate the pro-rata payment for renter and lender on the full amount.
        (uint256 renterAmount, uint256 lenderAmount) = _calculatePaymentProRata(
            amount,
            elapsedTime,
            totalTime
        );

        // Take a fee only on the renter's earned portion if the fee is on.
        if (fee != 0) {
            renterAmount -= _calculateFee(renterAmount);
        }

        // Send the lender portion of the payment (full refund of unused time).
        _safeTransfer(token, lender, lenderAmount);

        // Send the renter portion of the payment (minus protocol fee).
        _safeTransfer(token, renter, renterAmount);
    }

    function _settlePayment(
        Item[] calldata items,
        OrderType orderType,
        address lender,
        address renter,
        uint256 start,
        uint256 end
    ) internal {
        // Calculate the time values.
        uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - start;
        uint256 totalTime = end - start;

        // Determine whether the rental order has ended.
        bool isRentalOver = elapsedTime >= totalTime;

        // Loop through each item in the order.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < items.length; ++i) {
            // Get the item.
            Item memory item = items[i];

            // Check that the item is a payment.
            if (item.isERC20()) {
                uint256 paymentAmount = item.amount;

                // Effect: Decrease the token balance. Use the payment amount pre-fee
                // so that fees can be taken.
                _decreaseDeposit(item.token, item.amount);

                // If its a PAY order but the rental hasn't ended yet.
                if (orderType.isPayOrder() && !isRentalOver) {
                    // Interaction: a PAY order which hasnt ended yet. Payout is pro-rata.
                    _settlePaymentProRata(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        lender,
                        renter,
                        elapsedTime,
                        totalTime
                    );
                }
                // If its a PAY order and the rental is over, or, if its a BASE order.
                else if (
                    (orderType.isPayOrder() && isRentalOver) || orderType.isBaseOrder()
                ) {
                    // Take a fee on the payment amount if the fee is on.
                    if (fee != 0) {
                        paymentAmount -= _calculateFee(paymentAmount);
                    }

                    // Interaction: a pay order or base order which has ended. Payout is in full.
                    _settlePaymentInFull(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        item.settleTo,
                        lender,
                        renter
                    );
                } else {
                    revert Errors.Shared_OrderTypeNotSupported(uint8(orderType));
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

Apply the Checks-Effects-Interactions (CEI) pattern by removing the rental order records from `STORE` before calling `ESCRW.settlePayment` / `ESCRW.settlePaymentBatch` and `_reclaimRentedItems`, and add a `nonReentrant` guard to `PaymentEscrow.settlePayment`, `PaymentEscrow.settlePaymentBatch`, `Stop.stopRent`, and `Stop.stopRentBatch`.

Additionally, within `PaymentEscrow`, ensure state-modifying settlement entrypoints cannot be re-entered during `_settlePaymentProRata` and `_settlePaymentInFull`:

```solidity
    function _settlePayment(
        Item[] calldata items,
        OrderType orderType,
        address lender,
        address renter,
        uint256 start,
        uint256 end
    ) internal nonReentrant {
        // Calculate the time values.
        uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - start;
        uint256 totalTime = end - start;

        // Determine whether the rental order has ended.
        bool isRentalOver = elapsedTime >= totalTime;

        // Loop through each item in the order.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < items.length; ++i) {
            // Get the item.
            Item memory item = items[i];

            // Check that the item is a payment.
            if (item.isERC20()) {
                // Set a placeholder payment amount which can be reduced in the
                // presence of a fee.
                uint256 paymentAmount = item.amount;

                // Take a fee on the payment amount if the fee is on.
                if (fee != 0) {
                    // Calculate the new fee.
                    uint256 paymentFee = _calculateFee(paymentAmount);

                    // Adjust the payment amount by the fee.
                    paymentAmount -= paymentFee;
                }

                // Effect: Decrease the token balance. Use the payment amount pre-fee
                // so that fees can be taken.
                _decreaseDeposit(item.token, item.amount);

                // If its a PAY order but the rental hasn't ended yet.
                if (orderType.isPayOrder() && !isRentalOver) {
                    // Interaction: a PAY order which hasnt ended yet. Payout is pro-rata.
                    _settlePaymentProRata(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        lender,
                        renter,
                        elapsedTime,
                        totalTime
                    );
                }
                // If its a PAY order and the rental is over, or, if its a BASE order.
                else if (
                    (orderType.isPayOrder() && isRentalOver) || orderType.isBaseOrder()
                ) {
                    // Interaction: a pay order or base order which has ended. Payout is in full.
                    _settlePaymentInFull(
                        item.token,
                        paymentAmount,
                        item.settleTo,
                        lender,
                        renter
                    );
                } else {
                    revert Errors.Shared_OrderTypeNotSupported(uint8(orderType));
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

Implement a pull-over-push payment pattern (or a fallback claimable balance mapping when a transfer fails) in `PaymentEscrow` so that payment settlement during `stopRent` credits claimable balances (or catches failed transfers and records them as claimable) rather than reverting the rental termination transaction.

```solidity
                // If its a PAY order but the rental hasn't ended yet.
                if (orderType.isPayOrder() && !isRentalOver) {
                    // Interaction: a PAY order which hasnt ended yet. Payout is pro-rata.
                    (uint256 renterAmount, uint256 lenderAmount) = _calculatePaymentProRata(
                        paymentAmount,
                        elapsedTime,
                        totalTime
                    );
                    _trySafeTransferOrCredit(item.token, lender, lenderAmount);
                    _trySafeTransferOrCredit(item.token, renter, renterAmount);
                }
                // If its a PAY order and the rental is over, or, if its a BASE order.
                else if (
                    (orderType.isPayOrder() && isRentalOver) || orderType.isBaseOrder()
                ) {
                    // Interaction: a pay order or base order which has ended. Payout is in full.
                    address settleToAddress = item.settleTo == SettleTo.LENDER ? lender : renter;
                    _trySafeTransferOrCredit(
                        item.token,
                        settleToAddress,
                        paymentAmount
                    );
                } else {
                    revert Errors.Shared_OrderTypeNotSupported(uint8(orderType));
                }
```

Where `_trySafeTransferOrCredit` skips zero-amount transfers, attempts the ERC20 transfer, and if the transfer fails, increases `balanceOf[token]` and records the amount in a `claimable[user][token]` mapping for later withdrawal by the recipient.

Because Seaport executes token transfers before invoking `validateOrder` on the zone (making pre/post transfer balance measurement inside `validateOrder` impossible for a single execution without tracking cumulative unallocated balances or restricting tokens), either:
1. Enforce an explicit token allowlist in `_processBaseOrderConsideration` (and `_processPayOrderOffer`) so that only vetted, standard ERC20 tokens (non-fee-on-transfer, non-rebasing) can be used as payment items; or
2. Verify in `PaymentEscrow.increaseDeposit` that the contract's actual `ERC20(token).balanceOf(address(ESCRW))` is at least equal to the new cumulative tracked deposit balance for `token`, reverting in `_processBaseOrderConsideration` / `_rentFromZone` if a fee-on-transfer shortfall occurred.

```solidity
    function _processBaseOrderConsideration(
        Item[] memory rentalItems,
        ReceivedItem[] memory considerations,
        uint256 startIndex
    ) internal view {
        // Must be at least one consideration item.
        if (considerations.length == 0) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_ConsiderationCountZero();
        }

        // Process each consideration item.
        for (uint256 i; i < considerations.length; ++i) {
            // Get the consideration item.
            ReceivedItem memory consideration = considerations[i];

            // Only process a whitelisted, standard ERC20 item.
            if (!consideration.isERC20() || !STORE.isWhitelistedPaymentToken(consideration.token)) {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_SeaportItemTypeNotSupported(
                    consideration.itemType
                );
            }

            // An ERC20 consideration item is considered a payment to the lender upon
            // expiration of the rental order.
            rentalItems[i + startIndex] = Item({
                itemType: ItemType.ERC20,
                settleTo: SettleTo.LENDER,
                token: consideration.token,
                amount: consideration.amount,
                identifier: consideration.identifier
            });
        }
    }
```

Validate the `recipient` of every consideration item directly in `_processBaseOrderConsideration` (ensuring ERC20 payments are sent to `address(ESCRW)`) and validate the `PAYEE` order's consideration items and recipients in `_processPayeeOrderConsideration` (and ensure consideration/offer items are bound to actual executions):

```solidity
    function _processBaseOrderConsideration(
        Item[] memory rentalItems,
        ReceivedItem[] memory considerations,
        uint256 startIndex
    ) internal view {
        // Must be at least one consideration item.
        if (considerations.length == 0) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_ConsiderationCountZero();
        }

        // Process each consideration item.
        for (uint256 i; i < considerations.length; ++i) {
            // Get the consideration item.
            ReceivedItem memory consideration = considerations[i];

            // Only process an ERC20 item.
            if (!consideration.isERC20()) {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_SeaportItemTypeNotSupported(
                    consideration.itemType
                );
            }

            // Verify that the ERC20 consideration recipient is the payment escrow.
            if (consideration.recipient != address(ESCRW)) {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidConsiderationRecipient(
                    consideration.recipient
                );
            }

            // An ERC20 consideration item is considered a payment to the lender upon
            // expiration of the rental order.
            rentalItems[i + startIndex] = Item({
                itemType: ItemType.ERC20,
                settleTo: SettleTo.LENDER,
                token: consideration.token,
                amount: consideration.amount,
                identifier: consideration.identifier
            });
        }
    }

    function _processPayeeOrderConsideration(
        ReceivedItem[] memory considerations,
        address safe
    ) internal view {
        // Keep track of each item type.
        uint256 totalRentals;
        uint256 totalPayments;

        // Process each consideration item.
        for (uint256 i; i < considerations.length; ++i) {
            // Get the consideration item.
            ReceivedItem memory consideration = considerations[i];

            // Process an ERC20 item.
            if (consideration.isERC20()) {
                if (consideration.recipient != address(ESCRW)) {
                    revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidConsiderationRecipient(
                        consideration.recipient
                    );
                }
                totalPayments++;
            }
            // Process an ERC721 or ERC1155 consideration item.
            else if (consideration.isRental()) {
                if (consideration.recipient != safe) {
                    revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidConsiderationRecipient(
                        consideration.recipient
                    );
                }
                totalRentals++;
            }
            // Revert if unsupported item type.
            else {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_SeaportItemTypeNotSupported(
                    consideration.itemType
                );
            }
        }

        // PAYEE order consideration must have at least one rental and one payment.
        if (totalRentals == 0 || totalPayments == 0) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_ItemCountZero(totalRentals, totalPayments);
        }
    }
```

Include `order.rentalWallet` in the EIP-712 hash computation inside `Signer._deriveRentalOrderHash` (and ensure `_RENTAL_ORDER_TYPEHASH` includes `address rentalWallet` in the corresponding field position):

```solidity
    function _deriveRentalOrderHash(
        RentalOrder memory order
    ) internal view returns (bytes32) {
        // Create arrays for items and hooks.
        bytes32[] memory itemHashes = new bytes32[](order.items.length);
        bytes32[] memory hookHashes = new bytes32[](order.hooks.length);

        // Iterate over each item.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < order.items.length; ++i) {
            // Hash the item.
            itemHashes[i] = _deriveItemHash(order.items[i]);
        }

        // Iterate over each hook.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < order.hooks.length; ++i) {
            // Hash the hook.
            hookHashes[i] = _deriveHookHash(order.hooks[i]);
        }

        return
            keccak256(
                abi.encode(
                    _RENTAL_ORDER_TYPEHASH,
                    order.seaportOrderHash,
                    keccak256(abi.encodePacked(itemHashes)),
                    keccak256(abi.encodePacked(hookHashes)),
                    order.orderType,
                    order.lender,
                    order.renter,
                    order.rentalWallet,
                    order.startTimestamp,
                    order.endTimestamp
                )
            );
    }
```

Validate that each order's `offer` and `consideration` items are uniquely and completely accounted for in `seaportPayload.totalExecutions` (and cannot be reused across multiple orders in a batch or left unmatched in `matchAdvancedOrders`), or verify the actual ERC20 and NFT balance deltas on `ESCRW` and `expectedRentalSafe` per order.

Specifically, within `_executionInvariantChecks`, ensure that the executions match the exact items and amounts expected for the order and disallow shared/unmatched executions across multiple zone validations:

```solidity
    function _executionInvariantChecks(
        SpentItem[] memory offers,
        ReceivedItem[] memory considerations,
        OrderType orderType,
        ReceivedItem[] memory executions,
        address expectedRentalSafe,
        bytes32[] calldata orderHashes
    ) internal view {
        // Ensure each order in a batch only attributes its own executions.
        if (orderHashes.length > 1 && !orderType.isBaseOrder()) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidOrderBatch();
        }

        for (uint256 i = 0; i < executions.length; ++i) {
            ReceivedItem memory execution = executions[i];

            if (execution.isERC20()) {
                _checkExpectedRecipient(execution, address(ESCRW));
            } else if (execution.isRental()) {
                _checkExpectedRecipient(execution, expectedRentalSafe);
            } else {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_SeaportItemTypeNotSupported(
                    execution.itemType
                );
            }
        }

        // Verify that every offer item (for BASE and PAY orders) and consideration item
        // (for BASE orders) has a corresponding execution in `executions` with matching
        // token, identifier, and amount.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < offers.length; ++i) {
            SpentItem memory offer = offers[i];
            address expectedRecipient = offer.isERC20()
                ? address(ESCRW)
                : expectedRentalSafe;
            bool found;
            for (uint256 j = 0; j < executions.length; ++j) {
                ReceivedItem memory execution = executions[j];
                if (
                    execution.itemType == offer.itemType &&
                    execution.token == offer.token &&
                    execution.identifier == offer.identifier &&
                    execution.amount == offer.amount &&
                    execution.recipient == expectedRecipient
                ) {
                    found = true;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if (!found) {
                revert Errors.CreatePolicy_UnexpectedTokenRecipient(
                    offer.itemType,
                    offer.token,
                    offer.identifier,
                    offer.amount,
                    address(0),
                    expectedRecipient
                );
            }
        }
    }
```

Bind the signed `RentPayload` to the specific Seaport `orderHash` (`zoneParams.orderHash`) and ensure each `orderHash` (or signature) can only be used once in `validateOrder`. Additionally, commit to all `OrderMetadata` fields in `_deriveOrderMetadataHash`.

```solidity
    function validateOrder(
        ZoneParameters calldata zoneParams
    ) external override onlyRole("SEAPORT") returns (bytes4 validOrderMagicValue) {
        // Decode the signed rental zone payload from the extra data.
        (RentPayload memory payload, bytes memory signature) = abi.decode(
            zoneParams.extraData,
            (RentPayload, bytes)
        );

        // Ensure the order hash has not already been processed and matches the signed payload.
        if (STORE.orders(zoneParams.orderHash)) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_OrderAlreadyActive(zoneParams.orderHash);
        }

        // Create a payload of seaport data.
        SeaportPayload memory seaportPayload = SeaportPayload({
            orderHash: zoneParams.orderHash,
            zoneHash: zoneParams.zoneHash,
            offer: zoneParams.offer,
            consideration: zoneParams.consideration,
            totalExecutions: zoneParams.totalExecutions,
            fulfiller: zoneParams.fulfiller,
            offerer: zoneParams.offerer
        });

        // Check: The signature from the protocol signer has not expired.
        _validateProtocolSignatureExpiration(payload.expiration);

        // Check: The fulfiller is the intended fulfiller.
        _validateFulfiller(payload.intendedFulfiller, seaportPayload.fulfiller);

        // Recover the signer from the payload bound to zoneParams.orderHash.
        address signer = _recoverSignerFromPayload(
            _deriveRentPayloadHash(payload, zoneParams.orderHash),
            signature
        );

        // Check: The data matches the signature and that the protocol signer is the one that signed.
        if (!kernel.hasRole(signer, toRole("CREATE_SIGNER"))) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_UnauthorizedCreatePolicySigner();
        }

        // Initiate the rental using the rental manager.
        _rentFromZone(payload, seaportPayload);

        // Return the selector of validateOrder as the magic value.
        validOrderMagicValue = ZoneInterface.validateOrder.selector;
    }
```

Validate the recipients of `zoneParams.consideration` directly, and ensure that every item and amount in `zoneParams.offer` and `zoneParams.consideration` is backed by a verified transfer in `zoneParams.totalExecutions` (or verify actual token balance deltas on `ESCRW` and ownership/balance deltas on the recipient `rentalWallet`), rather than checking `totalExecutions` in isolation from `offer` and `consideration`.

```solidity
    function validateOrder(
        ZoneParameters calldata zoneParams
    ) external override onlyRole("SEAPORT") returns (bytes4 validOrderMagicValue) {
        // Decode the signed rental zone payload from the extra data.
        (RentPayload memory payload, bytes memory signature) = abi.decode(
            zoneParams.extraData,
            (RentPayload, bytes)
        );

        // Ensure all consideration items explicitly target the expected protocol recipients.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < zoneParams.consideration.length; ++i) {
            if (zoneParams.consideration[i].isERC20()) {
                _checkExpectedRecipient(zoneParams.consideration[i], address(ESCRW));
            } else if (zoneParams.consideration[i].isRental()) {
                _checkExpectedRecipient(
                    zoneParams.consideration[i],
                    payload.fulfillment.recipient
                );
            }
        }

        // Verify that all offer and consideration items were actually executed in totalExecutions.
        if (
            zoneParams.totalExecutions.length <
            zoneParams.offer.length + zoneParams.consideration.length
        ) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidExecutionCount();
        }

        // Create a payload of seaport data.
        SeaportPayload memory seaportPayload = SeaportPayload({
            orderHash: zoneParams.orderHash,
            zoneHash: zoneParams.zoneHash,
            offer: zoneParams.offer,
            consideration: zoneParams.consideration,
            totalExecutions: zoneParams.totalExecutions,
            fulfiller: zoneParams.fulfiller,
            offerer: zoneParams.offerer
        });
```

Include the expected consideration items (or expected consideration count / `seaportOrderHash`) in the signed `OrderMetadata` / `RentPayload` and validate in `Create.validateOrder` that `zoneParams.consideration` matches the signed order parameters without any fulfiller-appended items.

For example, bind `RentPayload` to `zoneParams.orderHash` and the expected `consideration.length` (or include `totalOriginalConsiderationItems` in `OrderMetadata` and enforce `zoneParams.consideration.length == payload.metadata.considerationLength`):

```solidity
    function validateOrder(
        ZoneParameters calldata zoneParams
    ) external override onlyRole("SEAPORT") returns (bytes4 validOrderMagicValue) {
        // Decode the signed rental zone payload from the extra data.
        (RentPayload memory payload, bytes memory signature) = abi.decode(
            zoneParams.extraData,
            (RentPayload, bytes)
        );

        // Ensure no additional consideration items (tips) were appended by the fulfiller.
        if (zoneParams.consideration.length != payload.metadata.expectedConsiderationLength) {
            revert Errors.CreatePolicy_InvalidConsiderationCount();
        }

        // Create a payload of seaport data.
        SeaportPayload memory seaportPayload = SeaportPayload({
            orderHash: zoneParams.orderHash,
            zoneHash: zoneParams.zoneHash,
            offer: zoneParams.offer,
            consideration: zoneParams.consideration,
            totalExecutions: zoneParams.totalExecutions,
            fulfiller: zoneParams.fulfiller,
            offerer: zoneParams.offerer
        });
```

findings.technical_details:
In `Storage.sol`, `rentedAssets[rentalId]` tracks the cumulative `uint256 amount` of actively rented tokens for a given `(recipient, token, identifier)` tuple (`RentalId`). While ERC721 tokens always have an amount of `1`, ERC1155 tokens are semi-fungible and can have arbitrary amounts rented out, or a rental safe can simultaneously hold both rented and self-owned balances of the same ERC1155 `identifier`, or multiple overlapping rentals of the same ERC1155 token ID.

However, in `Storage.isRentedOut` (lines 118–128):
```solidity
function isRentedOut(
    address recipient,
    address token,
    uint256 identifier
) external view returns (bool) {
    // calculate the rental ID
    RentalId rentalId = RentalUtils.getItemPointer(recipient, token, identifier);

    // Determine if there is a positive amount
    return rentedAssets[rentalId] != 0;
}
```
And in `Guard._checkTransaction` (lines 235–242):
```solidity
} else if (selector == e1155_safe_transfer_from_selector) {
    // Load the token ID from calldata.
    uint256 tokenId = uint256(
        _loadValueFromCalldata(data, e1155_safe_transfer_from_token_id_offset)
    );

    // Check if the selector is allowed.
    _revertSelectorOnActiveRental(selector, from, to, tokenId);
```

When a rental safe attempts to transfer an ERC1155 token via `safeTransferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 id, uint256 amount, bytes data)`, `Guard` only checks `STORE.isRentedOut(safe, token, tokenId)`. Because `isRentedOut` returns `true` whenever `rentedAssets[rentalId] != 0` instead of checking whether the remaining balance after the transfer is at least `rentedAssets[rentalId]`, any ERC1155 tokens of the same `tokenId` owned directly by the safe (or acquired during the rental) are completely frozen and cannot be transferred out until all active rentals for that `tokenId` have ended and been stopped.

Furthermore, if a malicious lender creates a long-duration `PAY` or `BASE` rental order for `amount = 1` (or `amount = 0` if allowed) of an ERC1155 token ID that the renter already holds in their safe (or receives as rewards in-game), all of the renter's own ERC1155 tokens of that ID become locked in the safe for the entire duration of the rental.

findings.remediation:
Update `Storage` and `Guard` so that for ERC1155 tokens, the guard checks whether the transfer `amount` would reduce the Safe's ERC1155 balance below `rentedAssets[rentalId]`, or expose the rented amount from `Storage` so `Guard` can validate `IERC1155(token).balanceOf(safe, tokenId) - transferAmount >= STORE.getRentedAmount(safe, token, tokenId)`.

```solidity
    function isRentedOut(
        address recipient,
        address token,
        uint256 identifier
    ) external view returns (bool) {
        // calculate the rental ID
        RentalId rentalId = RentalUtils.getItemPointer(recipient, token, identifier);

        // Determine if there is a positive amount
        return rentedAssets[rentalId] != 0;
    }

    function getRentedAmount(
        address recipient,
        address token,
        uint256 identifier
    ) external view returns (uint256) {
        RentalId rentalId = RentalUtils.getItemPointer(recipient, token, identifier);
        return rentedAssets[rentalId];
    }
```

findings.technical_details:
When `Factory.deployRentalSafe` deploys a new rental Safe proxy, it constructs an initializer payload calling `ISafe.setup` (lines 155–175) with:
1. A delegatecall payload to `Factory.initializeRentalSafe(address(stopPolicy), address(guardPolicy))` (line 151), which enables `stopPolicy` as a module and registers `guardPolicy` as the transaction guard via `ISafe.setGuard`.
2. `address(fallbackHandler)` (`TokenCallbackHandler`) as the initial `FallbackManager` handler (line 167) so the Safe can receive ERC721 and ERC1155 tokens.

In Gnosis Safe (`Safe.sol`), the transaction guard configured in `GuardManager` is only invoked during `Safe.execTransaction`. It is **not** invoked during `FallbackManager.fallback()`:

```solidity
fallback() external {
    bytes32 slot = FALLBACK_HANDLER_STORAGE_SLOT;
    assembly {
        let handler := sload(slot)
        if iszero(handler) {
            return(0, 0)
        }
        calldatacopy(0, 0, calldatasize())
        mstore(calldatasize(), shl(96, caller()))
        let success := call(gas(), handler, 0, 0, add(calldatasize(), 20), 0, 0)
        ...
    }
}
```

Whenever a call is made to the Safe proxy with a function selector that does not match any function defined on `Safe`, `FallbackManager.fallback()` loads the `handler` address from `FALLBACK_HANDLER_STORAGE_SLOT` and executes an unguarded `call` from the Safe (`msg.sender == safe`) to `handler` with the caller's calldata (plus 20 trailing bytes for `caller()`).

Furthermore, `FallbackManager.setFallbackHandler(address handler)` (`0xf08a0323`) is an `authorized` self-call on `Safe`. While `guardPolicy` restricts self-calls to `setGuard`, `enableModule`, and `disableModule` (defined in `RentalConstants.sol`), it does not restrict `setFallbackHandler`. Consequently, a rental Safe owner can:
1. Execute a standard Safe transaction (`execTransaction`) calling `safe.setFallbackHandler(address(nftContract))`, replacing the `TokenCallbackHandler` bound at line 167 with the address of a rented ERC721 or ERC1155 token contract.
2. Call `IERC721(safe).transferFrom(safe, attacker, tokenId)` (or `safeTransferFrom` / `setApprovalForAll`) directly on the Safe proxy.
3. Because `transferFrom` is not a function on `Safe`, execution falls through to `FallbackManager.fallback()`, which performs an unguarded `call` to `nftContract` with `msg.sender == safe`, transferring the rented NFT out of the Safe without triggering `guardPolicy`.

findings.remediation:
Ensure that the `fallbackHandler` bound during `Factory.deployRentalSafe` cannot be modified or abused after initialization. Specifically:
1. In the `guardPolicy` bound to the Safe at line 151 (and `RentalConstants.sol`), explicitly block calls to `FallbackManager.setFallbackHandler.selector` (`0xf08a0323`) so the Safe owner cannot overwrite `address(fallbackHandler)` set at line 167.
2. Alternatively, if a custom fallback handler is not changed post-deployment, validate inside the guard's `checkAfterExecution` / `checkTransaction` that the Safe's `FALLBACK_HANDLER_STORAGE_SLOT` remains equal to the trusted `address(fallbackHandler)` configured in `Factory.deployRentalSafe`:

```solidity
        // Delegate call from the safe so that the rental manager module and guard
        // (which must also disallow setFallbackHandler(address) / 0xf08a0323) are enabled
        // right after the safe is deployed.
        bytes memory data = abi.encodeCall(
            Factory.initializeRentalSafe,
            (address(stopPolicy), address(guardPolicy))
        );

        // Create gnosis initializer payload with the immutable TokenCallbackHandler.
        bytes memory initializerPayload = abi.encodeCall(
            ISafe.setup,
            (
                // owners array.
                owners,
                // number of signatures needed to execute transactions.
                threshold,
                // Address to direct the payload to.
                address(this),
                // Encoded call to execute.
                data,
                // Fallback manager address (must be locked against setFallbackHandler in guardPolicy).
                address(fallbackHandler),
                // Payment token.
                address(0),
                // Payment amount.
                0,
                // Payment receiver
                payable(address(0))
            )
        );
```

Allow the caller to supply an arbitrary `saltNonce` (or include a caller-controlled salt alongside `msg.sender` and `STORE.totalSafes()`) or use a salt derivation that cannot be deterministically locked for a given `(owners, threshold)` pair, so users can always bypass a pre-occupied `CREATE2` address on retry. Alternatively, include a caller-provided nonce in the salt calculation:

```solidity
