In `Stop._removeHooks`, instead of reverting when `STORE.hookOnStop(target)` is `false`, skip the `IHook(target).onStop(...)` execution for hooks that do not have `onStop` enabled (or have been disabled), allowing the rental to be cleanly stopped and assets reclaimed. Similarly, in `Create._addHooks`, only invoke `onStart` if `STORE.hookOnStart(target)` is enabled (while still requiring the hook itself to be an active hook on start).

Updated `Stop._removeHooks` in `smart-contracts/src/policies/Stop.sol`:

```solidity
    function _removeHooks(
        Hook[] calldata hooks,
        Item[] calldata rentalItems,
        address rentalWallet
    ) internal {
        // Define hook target, item index, and item.
        address target;
        uint256 itemIndex;
        Item memory item;

        // Loop through each hook in the payload.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < hooks.length; ++i) {
            // Get the hook address.
            target = hooks[i].target;

            // Only execute onStop if the hook has onStop enabled.
            if (STORE.hookOnStop(target)) {
                // Get the rental item index for this hook.
                itemIndex = hooks[i].itemIndex;

                // Get the rental item for this hook.
                item = rentalItems[itemIndex];

                // Make sure the item is a rented item.
                if (!item.isRental()) {
                    revert Errors.Shared_NonRentalHookItem(itemIndex);
                }

                // Call the hook with data about the rented item.
                try
                    IHook(target).onStop(
                        rentalWallet,
                        item.token,
                        item.identifier,
                        item.amount,
                        hooks[i].extraData
                    )
                {} catch Error(string memory revertReason) {
                    // Revert with reason given.
                    revert Errors.Shared_HookFailString(revertReason);
                } catch Panic(uint256 errorCode) {
                    // Convert solidity panic code to string.
                    string memory stringErrorCode = LibString.toString(errorCode);

                    // Revert with panic code.
                    revert Errors.Shared_HookFailString(
                        string.concat("Hook reverted: Panic code ", stringErrorCode)
                    );
                } catch (bytes memory revertData) {
                    // Fallback to an error that returns the byte data.
                    revert Errors.Shared_HookFailBytes(revertData);
                }
            }
        }
    }
```

findings.technical_details:
In `smart-contracts/src/modules/Storage.sol`, active rental orders are tracked using a boolean mapping `mapping(bytes32 orderHash => bool isActive) public orders`, while rented token balances per safe are tracked via `mapping(RentalId itemId => uint256 amount) public rentedAssets`.

When a rental is created in `Create._rentFromZone`, the contract derives `orderHash = _deriveRentalOrderHash(order)` and invokes `STORE.addRentals(orderHash, ...)`:

```solidity
function addRentals(
    bytes32 orderHash,
    RentalAssetUpdate[] memory rentalAssetUpdates
) external onlyByProxy permissioned {
    // Add the order to storage.
    orders[orderHash] = true;

    // Add the rented items to storage.
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < rentalAssetUpdates.length; ++i) {
        RentalAssetUpdate memory asset = rentalAssetUpdates[i];

        // Update the order hash for that item.
        rentedAssets[asset.rentalId] += asset.amount;
    }
}
```

Unlike `removeRentals` and `removeRentalsBatch`—which explicitly check `if (!orders[orderHash]) revert Errors.StorageModule_OrderDoesNotExist(orderHash)` before deleting the entry—`addRentals` performs no check on whether `orders[orderHash]` is already `true`.

A duplicate `orderHash` can occur when:
1. A Seaport order supporting partial fills (`PARTIAL_RESTRICTED`) is fulfilled multiple times in the same block (resulting in identical `seaportOrderHash`, `lender`, `renter`, `rentalWallet`, `items`, `startTimestamp`, and `endTimestamp`).
2. Identical rental order parameters are fulfilled within the same timestamp (`block.timestamp`) producing the same EIP-712 `RentalOrder` hash.

When `addRentals` is called a second time with an existing `orderHash`:
1. `orders[orderHash]` remains `true` (representing only a single active order in storage despite two active rentals).
2. `rentedAssets[asset.rentalId]` is incremented a second time by `asset.amount`.
3. `ESCRW.increaseDeposit` is called a second time in `Create._rentFromZone`, locking the second rental's ERC20 payment in escrow.

When `Stop.stopRent` (or `Stop.stopRentBatch`) is later executed:
1. Stopping the first rental succeeds: `Storage.removeRentals` deletes `orders[orderHash]` (setting it to `false`), decrements `rentedAssets[asset.rentalId]` once, reclaims the first set of rented items, and settles the first payment.
2. Stopping the second rental permanently reverts at `Storage.removeRentals` with `Errors.StorageModule_OrderDoesNotExist(orderHash)` because `orders[orderHash]` was already deleted during the first stop call.

findings.remediation:
Check whether `orders[orderHash]` is already active in `Storage.addRentals` and revert if the order hash already exists in storage.

```solidity
    function addRentals(
        bytes32 orderHash,
        RentalAssetUpdate[] memory rentalAssetUpdates
    ) external onlyByProxy permissioned {
        // The order must not already exist in storage.
        if (orders[orderHash]) {
            revert Errors.StorageModule_OrderAlreadyExists(orderHash);
        }

        // Add the order to storage.
        orders[orderHash] = true;

        // Add the rented items to storage.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < rentalAssetUpdates.length; ++i) {
            RentalAssetUpdate memory asset = rentalAssetUpdates[i];

            // Update the order hash for that item.
            rentedAssets[asset.rentalId] += asset.amount;
        }
    }
```

Include `order.rentalWallet` in `Signer._deriveRentalOrderHash` so that the derived hash matches the `RentalOrder` EIP-712 type definition and cryptographically binds the rental wallet address to `orderHash`.

```solidity
    function _deriveRentalOrderHash(
        RentalOrder memory order
    ) internal view returns (bytes32) {
        // Create arrays for items and hooks.
        bytes32[] memory itemHashes = new bytes32[](order.items.length);
        bytes32[] memory hookHashes = new bytes32[](order.hooks.length);

        // Iterate over each item.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < order.items.length; ++i) {
            // Hash the item.
            itemHashes[i] = _deriveItemHash(order.items[i]);
        }

        // Iterate over each hook.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < order.hooks.length; ++i) {
            // Hash the hook.
            hookHashes[i] = _deriveHookHash(order.hooks[i]);
        }

        return
            keccak256(
                abi.encode(
                    _RENTAL_ORDER_TYPEHASH,
                    order.seaportOrderHash,
                    keccak256(abi.encodePacked(itemHashes)),
                    keccak256(abi.encodePacked(hookHashes)),
                    order.orderType,
                    order.lender,
                    order.renter,
                    order.rentalWallet,
                    order.startTimestamp,
                    order.endTimestamp
                )
            );
    }
```

Update `_deriveHookHash`, `_deriveOrderMetadataHash`, and `_deriveRentalTypehashes` in `smart-contracts/src/packages/Signer.sol` to include all struct fields and strictly adhere to EIP-712 encoding rules:

```solidity
    function _deriveHookHash(Hook memory hook) internal view returns (bytes32) {
        // Derive and return the hook as specified by EIP-712.
        return
            keccak256(
                abi.encode(
                    _HOOK_TYPEHASH,
                    hook.target,
                    hook.itemIndex,
                    keccak256(hook.extraData)
                )
            );
    }

    function _deriveOrderMetadataHash(
        OrderMetadata memory metadata
    ) internal view returns (bytes32) {
        // Create array for hooks.
        bytes32[] memory hookHashes = new bytes32[](metadata.hooks.length);

        // Iterate over each hook.
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < metadata.hooks.length; ++i) {
            // Hash the hook
            hookHashes[i] = _deriveHookHash(metadata.hooks[i]);
        }

        // Derive and return the metadata hash as specified by EIP-712.
        return
            keccak256(
                abi.encode(
                    _ORDER_METADATA_TYPEHASH,
                    metadata.orderType,
                    metadata.rentDuration,
                    keccak256(abi.encodePacked(hookHashes)),
                    keccak256(metadata.emittedExtraData)
                )
            );
    }
```

