findings.technical_details:
When a transaction is executed by a rental Safe without an active transaction hook on the target contract, `Guard.checkTransaction` delegates validation to `_checkTransaction(msg.sender, to, data)` (line 343), where the `from` parameter represents `msg.sender` (the Safe initiating the transaction) and `to` represents the target token contract.

Inside `_checkTransaction` (specifically lines 203–226 and 235–242, including the highlighted `e721_safe_transfer_from_2_selector` and `e721_transfer_from_selector` branches on lines 212–226), the guard extracts only the `tokenId` from `data` at offset `0x64` (`e721_safe_transfer_from_2_token_id_offset` / `e721_transfer_from_token_id_offset`):

```solidity
} else if (selector == e721_safe_transfer_from_2_selector) {
    // Load the token ID from calldata.
    uint256 tokenId = uint256(
        _loadValueFromCalldata(data, e721_safe_transfer_from_2_token_id_offset)
    );

    // Check if the selector is allowed.
    _revertSelectorOnActiveRental(selector, from, to, tokenId);
} else if (selector == e721_transfer_from_selector) {
    // Load the token ID from calldata.
    uint256 tokenId = uint256(
        _loadValueFromCalldata(data, e721_transfer_from_token_id_offset)
    );

    // Check if the selector is allowed.
    _revertSelectorOnActiveRental(selector, from, to, tokenId);
}
```

`_revertSelectorOnActiveRental(selector, from, to, tokenId)` then queries `STORE.isRentedOut(safe, token, tokenId)` with `safe = from` (`msg.sender`). In `Storage.isRentedOut` (lines 118–128), the rental state lookup is scoped to the specific recipient Safe via `RentalUtils.getItemPointer(recipient, token, identifier)`:

```solidity
id = RentalId.wrap(keccak256(abi.encodePacked(recipient, token, identifier)));
```

However, in ERC-721 `transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId)` and `safeTransferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes data)` (as well as ERC-1155 `safeTransferFrom`), the actual owner of the token being transferred is the first calldata argument at offset `0x24`, not necessarily the transaction caller `msg.sender`. Because `_checkTransaction` fails to load the `from` (owner) address from calldata at offset `0x24` and instead checks `STORE.isRentedOut(msg.sender, to, tokenId)`, any transaction where `msg.sender` (`safeA`) calls `transferFrom(safeB, recipient, tokenId)` or `safeTransferFrom(safeB, recipient, tokenId, data)` checks whether `safeA` is renting `tokenId`. Since the rental record in `Storage.rentedAssets` is scoped to `safeB`, `STORE.isRentedOut(safeA, to, tokenId)` evaluates to `false`, allowing the transfer check to pass even though `(safeB, to, tokenId)` is actively rented.

findings.remediation:
In `Guard._checkTransaction`, load the `from` (token owner) address from `data` at offset `0x24` and check `_revertSelectorOnActiveRental` against the calldata `from` owner address (in addition to `msg.sender`), or unconditionally revert on `transferFrom` / `safeTransferFrom` calls when the calldata `from` address has an active rental:

```solidity
