        _reclaimRentedItems(order);

        // Interaction: Remove rentals from storage by computing the order hash before external ERC20 calls (CEI).
        STORE.removeRentals(
            _deriveRentalOrderHash(order),
            _convertToStatic(rentalAssetUpdates)
        );

        // Interaction: Settle ERC20 payments (using pull-over-push fallback in ESCRW so blacklisted recipients cannot revert stopRent).
        ESCRW.settlePayment(order);

        // Emit rental order stopped.
        _emitRentalOrderStopped(order.seaportOrderHash, msg.sender);
```

Additionally, within `PaymentEscrow._safeTransfer`, catch failed transfers and credit `claimable[token][to] += value` so that blacklisted or reverting recipients cannot block `ESCRW.settlePayment(order)`, and within `Reclaimer`, use `transferFrom` for ERC721 or escrow rejected tokens when `safeTransferFrom` fails so a reverting `order.lender` cannot block `stopRent`.

Enforce the Checks-Effects-Interactions (CEI) pattern in `Stop.stopRent` (and similarly in `Stop.stopRentBatch`) by calling `STORE.removeRentals` to validate and delete the rental order from storage before executing `_reclaimRentedItems` and `ESCRW.settlePayment`.

```solidity
