findings.technical_details:
In `src/libraries/logic/IsolateLogic.sol`, `executeIsolateRepay` computes the scaled repayment amount for each NFT loan directly from the user-supplied underlying amount `params.amounts[vars.nidx]` using `WadRayMath.rayDiv`:

```solidity
vars.isFullRepay = false;
vars.scaledRepayAmount = params.amounts[vars.nidx].rayDiv(debtGroupData.borrowIndex);
if (vars.scaledRepayAmount >= loanData.scaledAmount) {
  vars.scaledRepayAmount = loanData.scaledAmount;
  params.amounts[vars.nidx] = vars.scaledRepayAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex);
  vars.isFullRepay = true;
}
```

`WadRayMath.rayDiv(a, b)` computes `(a * 1e27 + b / 2) / b`, rounding half-up to the nearest integer. Because `debtGroupData.borrowIndex` grows above `1e27` (`RAY`) as interest accrues, performing `rayDiv` on the raw input prior to comparing against the loan's underlying debt produces four interrelated arithmetic flaws:

1. **Underlying-to-Scaled Conversion Inconsistencies & Precision-Sensitive Full-Repayment Boundaries:**
   The loan's actual underlying debt is `borrowAmount = loanData.scaledAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex)`. When `debtGroupData.borrowIndex > 1e27`, multiple distinct underlying amounts map to the same scaled value `loanData.scaledAmount` under `rayDiv`. Specifically, a caller supplying an amount strictly less than `borrowAmount` (up to `debtGroupData.borrowIndex / (2 * 1e27)` wei below `borrowAmount`) can still produce `vars.scaledRepayAmount == loanData.scaledAmount`. This prematurely triggers the `vars.scaledRepayAmount >= loanData.scaledAmount` branch, mutating `params.amounts[vars.nidx]` upward to `loanData.scaledAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex)`. Consequently, `VaultLogic.erc20TransferInLiquidity` pulls more ERC20 tokens from `params.msgSender` than requested in `params.amounts[vars.nidx]` (or reverts in `IsolateLending.isolateRepay` when paying with native tokens, because only `msg.value` matching the original `amounts` was wrapped into WETH). Furthermore, passing `type(uint256).max` to signal a full repayment overflows `mul(a, RAY)` inside `rayDiv` and reverts.

2. **Cumulative Rounding Drift in Partial Repayments:**
   Because `rayDiv` rounds half-up, any partial repayment `amount` where `(amount * 1e27) % borrowIndex >= (borrowIndex + 1) / 2` yields a `scaledRepayAmount` whose underlying equivalent `scaledRepayAmount.rayMul(borrowIndex)` exceeds the actual `amount` transferred into the pool. By splitting a repayment into multiple partial repayments chosen at rounding-up boundaries, a borrower reduces `loanData.scaledAmount` and `debtGroupData.totalScaledIsolateBorrow` by more value than the underlying tokens transferred into `debtAssetData.availableLiquidity`.

3. **Dust and Zero-Scaled Repayment Handling:**
   `ValidateLogic.validateIsolateRepayBasic` only enforces `inputParams.amounts[i] > 0`. When `debtGroupData.borrowIndex > 2e27`, any non-zero dust amount `params.amounts[vars.nidx] < debtGroupData.borrowIndex / (2 * 1e27)` evaluates to `vars.scaledRepayAmount = 0`. The function then deducts `0` from `loanData.scaledAmount` and `userScaledIsolateBorrow`, yet still adds `params.amounts[vars.nidx]` to `vars.totalRepayAmount` and transfers the tokens from the payer into the pool without reducing debt.

findings.remediation:
Compare the user-supplied underlying repayment amount against the loan's underlying borrow debt (`loanData.scaledAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex)`) first to determine whether the repayment is a full repayment, and require `vars.scaledRepayAmount > 0` for partial repayments (or recompute `params.amounts[vars.nidx] = vars.scaledRepayAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex)` so the transferred underlying amount matches the scaled debt reduction):

```solidity
    for (vars.nidx = 0; vars.nidx < params.nftTokenIds.length; vars.nidx++) {
      DataTypes.IsolateLoanData storage loanData = poolData.loanLookup[params.nftAsset][params.nftTokenIds[vars.nidx]];
      DataTypes.GroupData storage debtGroupData = debtAssetData.groupLookup[loanData.reserveGroup];

      ValidateLogic.validateIsolateRepayLoan(params, debtGroupData, loanData);

      uint256 borrowAmount = loanData.scaledAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex);
      if (params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= borrowAmount) {
        vars.scaledRepayAmount = loanData.scaledAmount;
        params.amounts[vars.nidx] = borrowAmount;
        vars.isFullRepay = true;
      } else {
        vars.scaledRepayAmount = params.amounts[vars.nidx].rayDiv(debtGroupData.borrowIndex);
        require(vars.scaledRepayAmount > 0, Errors.INVALID_AMOUNT);
        params.amounts[vars.nidx] = vars.scaledRepayAmount.rayMul(debtGroupData.borrowIndex);
        vars.isFullRepay = false;
      }
```

