findings.technical_details:
When an isolated NFT loan's debt exceeds `vars.thresholdPrice`, `IsolateLogic.executeIsolateAuction` transitions the loan from `Constants.LOAN_STATUS_ACTIVE` to `Constants.LOAN_STATUS_AUCTION` and records the initiator as `loanData.firstBidder` (`src/libraries/logic/IsolateLogic.sol:238`):

```solidity
// record first bid state
loanData.firstBidder = params.msgSender;
loanData.loanStatus = Constants.LOAN_STATUS_AUCTION;
loanData.bidStartTimestamp = uint40(block.timestamp);
```

The purpose of recording `loanData.firstBidder` is to compensate the liquidator who initiates the auction if the borrower subsequently redeems the NFT during `auctionDuration`. Specifically, in `IsolateLogic.executeIsolateRedeem` (`src/libraries/logic/IsolateLogic.sol:346-354`), the borrower (`tokenData.owner`) must pay `vars.bidFines[vars.nidx]` (computed by `GenericLogic.calculateNftLoanBidFine`) to `loanData.firstBidder`:

```solidity
if (loanData.firstBidder != address(0)) {
  // transfer bid fine from borrower to the first bidder
  VaultLogic.erc20TransferBetweenWallets(
    params.asset,
    params.msgSender,
    loanData.firstBidder,
    vars.bidFines[vars.nidx]
  );
}
```

Although `ValidateLogic.validateIsolateAuctionLoan` (`src/libraries/logic/ValidateLogic.sol:545`) checks `require(inputParams.msgSender != tokenData.owner, Errors.INVALID_CALLER)`, this check is trivially bypassed using a secondary address controlled by the borrower (`sybil != tokenData.owner`). This enables two economic attacks on the first-bidder incentive:

1. **Free-Option Griefing Against Genuine Liquidators**: As soon as the loan becomes liquidatable (or by front-running a liquidator's initial bid transaction), the borrower calls `isolateAuction` from a secondary address `sybil` with the minimum valid bid (`max(vars.borrowAmount, vars.liquidatePrice)`). `loanData.firstBidder` and `loanData.lastBidder` are both set to `sybil`. When a genuine liquidator subsequently places a higher bid (entering the `else` branch at line 241), `sybil`'s entire bid is immediately refunded at lines 261-263 (`VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmount`), leaving the genuine liquidator's capital locked in escrow for the remainder of `auctionDuration` while the borrower has zero capital locked. However, `loanData.firstBidder` remains `sybil`. The borrower can then call `isolateRedeem` at any time before `vars.auctionEndTimestamp`, paying `vars.bidFines[vars.nidx]` from `tokenData.owner` back to `sybil` (zero net penalty) while the genuine liquidator receives only their principal back and zero `bidFine` reward.
2. **Penalty-Free Partial Debt Reduction via Atomic Self-Redemption**: When front-running a liquidator's first bid, the borrower can atomically call `isolateAuction` from `sybil` and `isolateRedeem` from `tokenData.owner`, repaying only `vars.borrowAmount.percentMul(nftAssetData.redeemThreshold)` to restore the loan's health while routing the mandatory `bidFine` back to `sybil`.

findings.remediation:
Distribute a portion (or all) of the redemption `bidFine` to `loanData.lastBidder` (who actively locks capital at the highest bid price) or require a non-refundable protocol fee share on redemption so that self-bidding via a secondary account always incurs a real economic cost, and ensure subsequent bidders in the `else` branch are also required to meet `vars.liquidatePrice` and receive fair incentive compensation.

```solidity
      // first time bid
      if (loanData.loanStatus == Constants.LOAN_STATUS_ACTIVE) {
        // loan's accumulated debt must exceed threshold (heath factor below 1.0)
        require(vars.borrowAmount > vars.thresholdPrice, Errors.ISOLATE_BORROW_NOT_EXCEED_LIQUIDATION_THRESHOLD);

        // bid price must greater than borrow debt
        require(params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= vars.borrowAmount, Errors.ISOLATE_BID_PRICE_LESS_THAN_BORROW);

        // bid price must greater than liquidate price
        require(params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= vars.liquidatePrice, Errors.ISOLATE_BID_PRICE_LESS_THAN_LIQUIDATION_PRICE);

        // record first bid state
        loanData.firstBidder = params.msgSender;
        loanData.loanStatus = Constants.LOAN_STATUS_AUCTION;
        loanData.bidStartTimestamp = uint40(block.timestamp);
      } else {
        vars.auctionEndTimestamp = loanData.bidStartTimestamp + nftAssetData.auctionDuration;
        require(block.timestamp <= vars.auctionEndTimestamp, Errors.ISOLATE_BID_AUCTION_DURATION_HAS_END);

        // bid price must greater than borrow debt and current liquidate price
        require(params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= vars.borrowAmount, Errors.ISOLATE_BID_PRICE_LESS_THAN_BORROW);
        require(params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= vars.liquidatePrice, Errors.ISOLATE_BID_PRICE_LESS_THAN_LIQUIDATION_PRICE);

        // update incentive recipient to active highest bidder who locks capital
        loanData.firstBidder = params.msgSender;
```

findings.technical_details:
When an isolated NFT loan becomes undercollateralized, liquidators can bid on the NFT collateral via `IsolateLiquidation.isolateAuction`, which delegates to `IsolateLogic.executeIsolateAuction`.

During the first bid on an active loan (`loanData.loanStatus == Constants.LOAN_STATUS_ACTIVE`), `loanData.lastBidder` and `loanData.bidAmount` are recorded, and the bid amount is transferred into escrow via `VaultLogic.erc20TransferInBidAmount` (line 269).

When a subsequent bidder attempts to outbid the current highest bidder during the auction window, `IsolateLogic.executeIsolateAuction` records the new bidder and immediately pushes the previous bid refund to `vars.oldLastBidder` at lines 260–263:

```solidity
// record last bid state
loanData.lastBidder = params.msgSender;
loanData.bidAmount = params.amounts[vars.nidx];

// transfer last bid amount to previous bidder from escrow
if ((vars.oldLastBidder != address(0)) && (vars.oldBidAmount > 0)) {
  VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmount(debtAssetData, vars.oldLastBidder, vars.oldBidAmount);
}
```

`VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmount` (lines 480–494 of `VaultLogic.sol`) executes `IERC20Upgradeable(asset).safeTransfer(to, amount)` to `vars.oldLastBidder`.

This push-based refund mechanism introduces a recipient-dependent liveness failure in two scenarios:
1. **Blacklisted Address (e.g., USDT / USDC):** The protocol explicitly supports tokens with blacklist functionality such as USDT (as seen in `TestIntIsolateAuction.t.sol`). If `vars.oldLastBidder` becomes blacklisted after placing a bid, `safeTransfer(vars.oldLastBidder, vars.oldBidAmount)` will unconditionally revert.
2. **Tokens with Recipient Callbacks (e.g., ERC777 / ERC1363):** If the underlying debt asset invokes a recipient hook on `transfer` (such as `tokensReceived` in ERC777), a malicious `vars.oldLastBidder` contract can revert inside the callback whenever `erc20TransferOutBidAmount` attempts to refund its bid.

Because `executeIsolateAuction` requires the outgoing transfer to `vars.oldLastBidder` to succeed, no other liquidator can place a higher bid on the loan. Moreover, `executeIsolateRedeem` (line 343) also calls `VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmount(debtAssetData, loanData.lastBidder, loanData.bidAmount)`, preventing the borrower from redeeming the loan. Once `auctionEndTimestamp` passes, `executeIsolateLiquidate` transfers the NFT to the winning bidder without transferring the ERC20 bid back to `lastBidder`, allowing the bidder to acquire the NFT at the initial discounted liquidation price without competition.

findings.remediation:
Replace the synchronous push transfer in `executeIsolateAuction` with a pull-based refund mechanism (or wrap the low-level token transfer in a fallback that credits claimable balances if the direct transfer fails), so that a reverting or blacklisted `oldLastBidder` cannot block subsequent bids.

```solidity
      // record last bid state
      loanData.lastBidder = params.msgSender;
      loanData.bidAmount = params.amounts[vars.nidx];

      // credit or safely refund last bid amount to previous bidder from escrow
      if ((vars.oldLastBidder != address(0)) && (vars.oldBidAmount > 0)) {
        VaultLogic.erc20CreditOrTransferOutBidAmount(debtAssetData, vars.oldLastBidder, vars.oldBidAmount);
      }

      vars.totalBidAmount += params.amounts[vars.nidx];
```

Where `erc20CreditOrTransferOutBidAmount` either records `vars.oldBidAmount` in a mapping of claimable refunds (`mapping(address => uint256) claimableBidRefunds`) for `vars.oldLastBidder` to withdraw separately, or attempts the transfer with a `try/catch` (and bounded gas) and falls back to storing the claimable refund on failure.

Calculate `vars.minBidDelta` as a percentage of the current highest bid `loanData.bidAmount` (which is guaranteed to be `>= vars.borrowAmount`), and enforce a strict progression check (`>` when `minBidDelta == 0`, or clamp `vars.minBidDelta` to a minimum of `1`):

```solidity
        // bid price must greater than highest bid + delta
        vars.minBidDelta = loanData.bidAmount.percentMul(PercentageMath.ONE_PERCENTAGE_FACTOR);
        if (vars.minBidDelta == 0) {
          vars.minBidDelta = 1;
        }
        require(
          params.amounts[vars.nidx] >= (loanData.bidAmount + vars.minBidDelta),
          Errors.ISOLATE_BID_PRICE_LESS_THAN_HIGHEST_PRICE
        );
```

Pass `vars.totalBorrowAmount` (instead of `vars.totalBorrowAmount + vars.totalExtraAmount`) to `InterestLogic.updateInterestRates`, and transfer `vars.totalBorrowAmount - vars.totalExtraAmount` (instead of `vars.totalBorrowAmount`) from `totalBidAmout` to `availableLiquidity` in `VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmountToLiqudity`.

```solidity
    // update interest rate according latest borrow amount (utilizaton)
    InterestLogic.updateInterestRates(poolData, debtAssetData, vars.totalBorrowAmount, 0);

    // bid already in pool and now repay the borrow but need to increase liquidity
    VaultLogic.erc20TransferOutBidAmountToLiqudity(
      debtAssetData,
      vars.totalBorrowAmount - vars.totalExtraAmount
    );

    if (vars.totalExtraAmount > 0) {
      // transfer underlying asset from liquidator to pool
      VaultLogic.erc20TransferInLiquidity(debtAssetData, params.msgSender, vars.totalExtraAmount);
    }
```

Unlock the ERC721 token by resetting its `lockerAddr` to `address(0)` in `IsolateLogic.executeIsolateLiquidate` when settling each liquidated loan, matching the cleanup logic in `executeIsolateRepay`.

```solidity
