findings.technical_details:
In `src/Float128.sol`, `toPackedFloat(int mantissa, int exponent)` normalizes any non-zero input into either a 38-digit medium mantissa (`M`) or a 72-digit large mantissa (`L`). According to the documentation, the library is designed to accurately handle up to 72 significant digits and prioritizes precision over gas efficiency.

When `mantissa` is already 72 digits (`MIN_L_DIGIT_NUMBER <= mantissa <= MAX_L_DIGIT_NUMBER`), lines 1125–1129 preserve all 72 digits by setting `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` regardless of `exponent`.

However, when `mantissa` has between 39 and 71 digits (`MAX_DIGITS_M < digitsMantissa < MAX_DIGITS_L`), execution enters the normalization branch at lines 1095–1115:

```solidity
mantissaMultiplier := sub(digitsMantissa, MAX_DIGITS_M)
let isResultL := slt(MAXIMUM_EXPONENT, add(exponent, mantissaMultiplier))
if isResultL {
    mantissaMultiplier := sub(mantissaMultiplier, DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)
    float := or(float, MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK)
}
exponent := add(exponent, mantissaMultiplier)
let negativeMultiplier := and(TWO_COMPLEMENT_SIGN_MASK, mantissaMultiplier)
if negativeMultiplier {
    mantissa := mul(mantissa, exp(BASE, sub(0, mantissaMultiplier)))
}
if iszero(negativeMultiplier) {
    mantissa := div(mantissa, exp(BASE, mantissaMultiplier))
}
```

For `39 <= digitsMantissa <= 71`, `mantissaMultiplier = digitsMantissa - 38` is positive (`1 <= mantissaMultiplier <= 33`). If `exponent + mantissaMultiplier <= MAXIMUM_EXPONENT` (`-18`), `isResultL` evaluates to `0`. Instead of scaling the mantissa up to 72 digits (`L` format) to preserve its significant digits, `toPackedFloat` keeps `mantissaMultiplier > 0` (`negativeMultiplier == 0`) and executes line 1113:

```solidity
mantissa := div(mantissa, exp(BASE, mantissaMultiplier))
```

This integer division truncates the least significant `digitsMantissa - 38` digits of `mantissa`, causing silent loss of up to 33 digits of precision. Additionally, if `digitsMantissa > 72` and `exponent + mantissaMultiplier <= MAXIMUM_EXPONENT`, it downscales all the way to 38 digits instead of 72 digits.

