findings.technical_details:
The `Float128` library enforces a canonical normalization and mantissa-size autoscaling rule governed by `MAXIMUM_EXPONENT = -18`:
- A normalized number whose 38-digit (medium-mantissa, `M`) representation has an exponent `<= MAXIMUM_EXPONENT` (`-18`) must be stored with a 38-digit mantissa and `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` cleared (`0`).
- A normalized number whose 38-digit (`M`) representation would have an exponent `> MAXIMUM_EXPONENT` (`-18`) — equivalent to a 72-digit (`L`) exponent `> MAXIMUM_EXPONENT - int(DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)` (`-52`) — must be stored with a 72-digit mantissa and `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` set (`1`).

In `Float128.toPackedFloat` (`src/Float128.sol`), normalization is split into three branches:

1. **Unnormalized mantissa (lines 1095–1115):** When `mantissa` has neither 38 nor 72 digits, `toPackedFloat` computes the 38-digit exponent `add(exponent, mantissaMultiplier)` (where `mantissaMultiplier = digitsMantissa - 38`) and checks `slt(MAXIMUM_EXPONENT, add(exponent, mantissaMultiplier))`. Only when this 38-digit exponent exceeds `MAXIMUM_EXPONENT` (`-18`) does it encode the value as a 72-digit `L` float; otherwise, it scales `mantissa` to 38 digits (`M`).
2. **38-digit mantissa (lines 1116–1124):** When `mantissa` has 38 digits (`MIN_M_DIGIT_NUMBER <= mantissa <= MAX_M_DIGIT_NUMBER`) and `exponent > MAXIMUM_EXPONENT`, `toPackedFloat` upscales `mantissa` by `BASE_TO_THE_DIGIT_DIFF` (`10**34`), subtracts `DIGIT_DIFF_L_M` (`34`) from `exponent`, and sets `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK`. If `exponent <= MAXIMUM_EXPONENT`, it leaves the 38-digit mantissa in `M` format.
3. **72-digit mantissa (lines 1125–1129):**
   ```solidity
   } else if ((mantissa <= int(MAX_L_DIGIT_NUMBER) && mantissa >= int(MIN_L_DIGIT_NUMBER))) {
       assembly {
           float := add(float, MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK)
       }
   }
   ```
   When `mantissa` has 72 digits, `toPackedFloat` unconditionally sets `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` without checking whether the equivalent 38-digit exponent `exponent + int(DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)` is `<= MAXIMUM_EXPONENT` (i.e., `exponent <= -52`).

Consequently, any 72-digit mantissa paired with an exponent `<= -52` is encoded as a 72-digit `L` float instead of being downscaled to a 38-digit `M` float (`mantissa / 10**34` with `exponent + 34`). Because `Float128.eq` compares raw `packedFloat` bitmaps directly (`packedFloat.unwrap(a) == packedFloat.unwrap(b)`), two `packedFloat` values representing the exact same number evaluate as unequal if one was constructed from a 72-digit mantissa with `exponent <= -52` and the other was constructed from any other digit length or returned by an arithmetic operation (`add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div`, `sqrt`), all of which downscale to `M` format when the `L` exponent is `<= -52`.

findings.remediation:
In `Float128.toPackedFloat`, check whether a 72-digit mantissa has `exponent > MAXIMUM_EXPONENT - int(DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)` before setting `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK`; otherwise, downscale `mantissa` by `BASE_TO_THE_DIGIT_DIFF` and increment `exponent` by `DIGIT_DIFF_L_M`:

```solidity
            } else if (
                (mantissa <= int(MAX_M_DIGIT_NUMBER) && mantissa >= int(MIN_M_DIGIT_NUMBER)) &&
                exponent > MAXIMUM_EXPONENT
            ) {
                assembly {
                    mantissa := mul(mantissa, BASE_TO_THE_DIGIT_DIFF)
                    exponent := sub(exponent, DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)
                    float := add(float, MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK)
                }
            } else if ((mantissa <= int(MAX_L_DIGIT_NUMBER) && mantissa >= int(MIN_L_DIGIT_NUMBER))) {
                if (exponent > MAXIMUM_EXPONENT - int(DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)) {
                    assembly {
                        float := add(float, MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK)
                    }
                } else {
                    assembly {
                        mantissa := div(mantissa, BASE_TO_THE_DIGIT_DIFF)
                        exponent := add(exponent, DIGIT_DIFF_L_M)
                    }
                }
            }
```

