findings.technical_details:
In `src/Float128.sol`, a `packedFloat` encodes either a 38-digit medium (`M`) mantissa with bit 241 (`MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK`, line 16) cleared, or a 72-digit large (`L`) mantissa with `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` set. All arithmetic, comparison, square root, and logarithm operations inspect `and(x, MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK)` to determine whether the mantissa has 38 or 72 significant digits.

In `Float128.add` (lines 180–213) and `Float128.sub` (lines 382–415), when `isSubtraction` is true, the intermediate magnitude `addition` can have anywhere from 1 to 76 digits while `r` only holds the unnormalized result exponent `rExp` and sign bit (`MANTISSA_SIGN_MASK`), with `MANTISSA_L_FLAG_MASK` unset:

```solidity
